Install AWS CLI

Objective:
Install AWS CLI to enable command-line interaction with AWS services.

Why:
Jenkins will use AWS CLI to authenticate and push Docker images to Amazon ECR.

Command:
sudo snap install aws-cli --classic
What is Snap?
Think:
apt
Traditional Ubuntu package manager.
Old Style

snap
Modern package manager.
Containerized Applications
Auto Updates

Verification:
aws --version

Expected Output:
aws-cli/2.x.x

Learning:
AWS CLI enables infrastructure and deployment automation through terminal commands.
